<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Diagram of a tumor microenvironment shows various cell types and barriers contributing to impaired antitumor immunity, including stromal-ECM barriers, tumor cell nests, impaired antigen presentation, regulatory lymphoid niches, exhausted cytotoxic T lymphocytes, suppressive myeloid niches, and hypoxic metabolic conditions.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt (Infographic showing immunosuppressive tumor-associated macrophages at the center influenced by microenvironment cues on the left, such as tumor-derived, stromal-derived, ECM-mechanical, hypoxic metabolic, nutrient stress, and lipid-rich conditions, leading to functions on the right including impaired antigen presentation, CTL dysfunction, Treg support, metabolic restriction, matrix remodelling, and angiogenesis.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
